# Festival of Embers casts "instant and sorcery spells": Bot1's Chain Lightning (a sorcery, Bot2 17) is cast again from its graveyard on turn 5, for {R} and 1 life
# (Bot1 19, Bot2 14), and is exiled. Its Memnite, killed by Bot2's Lightning Bolt on turn 2, sits in the graveyard too but is no instant or sorcery, so it cannot be
# cast from there. Bot2's own Bolt, in Bot2's graveyard, is not Bot1's to cast and stays there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Chain Lightning
Memnite
Festival of Embers
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chain Lightning.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Chain Lightning
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Festival of Embers.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot1.Graveyard.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Graveyard.Chain Lightning.Cast(Bot2; Ability: During your turn)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 14
Exile = Chain Lightning
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
